        }
      ]
    },
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "No. Only the curved surface is doubled, and the circular ends stay the same, so the total is not doubled.",
      "worked": "The radius stays the same, so the area of the two circular ends, $2\\pi r^2$, stays the same. Doubling the height doubles only the curved surface area, $2\\pi rh$. Therefore the total surface area is not doubled.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
